 * 5. Switch to Member B (a separate ordinary member with no moderator/admin rights).
 * 6. Attempt to delete the post edit audit event as Member B using the moderator-only API.
 * 7. Confirm that the deletion request is denied by the system with a permission error/forbidden access (test for error thrown).
 * 8. (Optional) Ensure the post edit event still exists by checking that record is not deleted (if a public API exists for this, otherwise skip per available API surface).
 *
